\DOC GEN_X86_ADD_RETURN_STACK_TAC

\TYPE {GEN_X86_ADD_RETURN_STACK_TAC : thm * (thm option array) -> thm -> term -> int -> int * int -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Proves an {ensures} specification for a subroutine that saves callee-saved
registers and allocates stack space, deriving it from a given core
specification about the subroutine body.

\DESCRIBE
{GEN_X86_ADD_RETURN_STACK_TAC execth coreth reglist stackoff (n,m)} takes
{execth : thm * (thm option array)}, the execution/decoding data for the
program, including a theorem giving the length of the byte list;
{coreth : thm}, the correctness theorem for the subroutine's core, stated for
the inner entry/exit addresses; {reglist : term}, a term list of the
callee-saved registers the wrapper preserves; {stackoff : int}, the size of the
stack frame subtracted from the stack pointer; and {(n,m) : int * int},
instruction counts for the wrapper's prologue and epilogue. It applies to a
universally quantified (and sometimes outermost existentially quantified) goal
of the form {A ?- ... ensures x86 ...} relating entry at the program's start
with a stack-allocating wrapper and the return address. The goal is either
closed outright or reduced to a single subgoal in which all the outer
quantifiers have been stripped, the non-overlapping side conditions and the
derived facts about the final machine state (register and flag reads, memory
reads at the saved-register slots, the frame condition, and the accumulated
event trace) have been added as assumptions, and the conclusion is the
remaining existential claim about the event trace.
{
           A ?- t
      ==============================  GEN_X86_ADD_RETURN_STACK_TAC execth coreth reglist stackoff (n,m)
           (no subgoals)
}
\noindent         A ?- t    ==============================
GEN_X86_ADD_RETURN_STACK_TAC execth coreth reglist stackoff (n,m)       A, h1
... hn ?- u ```

where {h1 ... hn} are the added hypotheses and {u} is the residual part of the
specification's postcondition.

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only these two outcomes, on goals stating x86
subroutine {ensures} specifications of this shape.

\ENDDOC
